  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The abstract does not disclose the sample size, the duration of the intervention, or whether these changed beliefs translate into actual inclusive classroom practices.",
      "what": "This study evaluated a university-based teacher training course designed to improve inclusive geography teaching beliefs and self-efficacy. Using a pre-post experimental design with an untreated control group, the researchers analyzed changes in prospective teachers' beliefs using repeated measures ANOVA and MANCOVA.",
      "why": "The intervention demonstrates that targeted university coursework can successfully shift teacher attitudes and significantly boost their self-efficacy regarding inclusive geography instruction, providing a tested model for teacher education curricula."
    }
